00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:03.120
Okay, so a user whose username

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:06.950
is just a seemingly random
series of letters asks,

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:09.080
what does the Central Intelligence Agency

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:10.010
have to do with this?

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:11.960
This sounds like more of an FBI matter?

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:13.830
Well, that is a great question.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.570
With respect to John Bolton.

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:17.560
Remember, he was the
National Security Adviser.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:20.480
So he was privy to a lot
of different information,

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:23.600
and worked with a lot of
different governmental agencies.

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:26.210
And the thing about the
prepublication review process

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:28.990
is that when there is
sensitive information,

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:30.470
or potentially classified information,

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.410
or potentially prohibited information,

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:36.420
instead of having one
agency do the review,

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:39.140
you often give the source material

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:42.350
to a bunch of different
agencies that are responsible

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:44.240
for that particular thing.

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:47.440
When he submitted his
book to the government,

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.740
the National Security Council
for prepublication review,

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:53.790
the NSC probably gave that
book to other agencies

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:57.320
so they can do their own
review, including the CIA.

00:14:57.320 --> 00:15:00.040
So that is one of the
reasons why we have sued all

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:00.990
these different agencies.

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:04.760
Is because they had access
to the book, presumably.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:07.890
And they are subject to FOIA.

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:10.880
And we wanna know what concerns they had,

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.440
what they told John Bolton to remove,

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:16.210
and what they said he could not publish.

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:17.730
So that's why in this particular case,

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:21.470
the CIA and not the FBI
is the particular agency

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:23.760
to get FOIA-ied in this particular case.

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:26.900
Okay, let's see user
Elizabeth Henning asks,

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:29.500
this seems like the kind
of lawsuit newspapers file

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:31.520
when their FOIA requests
are ignored or denied

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:33.840
and this is a matter of
considerable national interest.

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:37.100
Are any press outlets
joining you in the suit?

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:39.640
So Elizabeth, you're absolutely right on,

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:41.600
this is exactly that kind of suit.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.270
And there are other organizations

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:45.250
that do this kind of thing all the time.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:48.560
In particular, one I'm particularly
fond of is called CREW.

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:50.370
It's the Citizens for Responsibility

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:51.950
and Ethics in Washington.

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:55.240
They do a great job of
really getting to the heart

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:56.450
of important matters,

00:15:56.450 --> 00:16:00.960
FOIA-ing them and being capable
of taking those to court.

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.010
To be able to enforce their FOIA requests.

00:16:03.010 --> 00:16:05.170
So if you believe in the mission

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:07.120
of governmental transparency,

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:09.620
and you believe in the mission
of this particular lawsuit,

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:13.200
I would highly recommend
checking out Crew and MuckRock,

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:15.830
they do this kind of thing all the time.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.790
This lawsuit is different,

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:19.070
I hinted at that before.

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:21.080
Because we're taking the the NSC,

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:22.750
the National Security Council head on.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:27.740
Which is something that a
lot of these organizations

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:30.680
aren't willing to do for various reasons.

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:33.130
We think this particular incidence

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:37.080
with John Bolton especially
given the impeachment saga

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:38.980
and now John Bolton's book,

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:41.440
and potentially the election in November,

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:42.280
incredibly important.

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:44.340
And so we're willing to put in the time

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:46.230
and go further with this lawsuit

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:50.489
than often some organizations are.

00:16:50.489 --> 00:16:51.810
Some for very good reasons,

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:54.320
but we wholeheartedly
believe in the mission

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:57.900
of those other organizations
in fighting corruption

00:16:57.900 --> 00:17:00.290
that you need transparency
from the government.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:02.960
Especially when things are this important

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.480
and the stakes are so high.

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:07.640
Alright, so that takes me to user Rockery,

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:10.940
which asks How do you even
subpoena a government agency?

